      "id": "code-review-reality-server-sso-sessions-unbounded-map",
      "type": "code-review-finding",
      "source": "review-2026-07-31 (reality-server segment, pm-backend expert)",
      "score_delta": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "candidate_vector": "security",
      "evidence": "backend/servers/reality-server/src/state.rs:841 \u2014 `pub sso_sessions: Arc<Mutex<HashMap<String, PendingSsoSession>>>` PKCE-flow store: inserted on every unauth GET /api/v1/sso/login (routes/sso.rs:94) and only removed on successful matching /sso/callback (routes/sso.rs:235-244). Nothing sweeps 10-minute expiry, so abandoned logins leak forever \u2014 unauthenticated flood \u2192 memory-exhaustion DoS + global-mutex contention. Sibling SsoTokenService (state.rs:453-460) and TokenValidationCache (state.rs:679-706) already fixed this pattern; sso_sessions was missed. Fix: mirror SsoTokenService `.retain(|_,t| now - created_at < 10min)` sweep on insert + cap size."
    },
    {
      "id": "code-review-reality-server-login-user-enumeration-oracle",
      "type": "code-review-finding",
      "source": "review-2026-07-31 (reality-server segment, pm-backend expert)",
      "score_delta": 2,
      "confidence": "high",
      "candidate_vector": "security",
      "evidence": "backend/servers/reality-server/src/handlers/users/mod.rs:263 login() has three distinguishable outcomes on public unauth POST /api/v1/users/login: (a) unknown email \u2192 immediate `Invalid email or password` no argon2 (line 255); (b) known email + no password_hash (SSO-only) \u2192 literal `Account uses SSO login` (line 263) discloses email exists + is SSO; (c) known + password \u2192 argon2 then generic error. Two enumeration oracles: distinct SSO string + timing gap between (a)/(b) vs (c). Same handler documents anti-enumeration for password reset (mod.rs:22-24) but login is inconsistent. Fix: (1) collapse SSO branch to generic error; (2) fixed-cost dummy argon2 in unknown-email path for uniform timing."
    },
    {
