      "type": "code-review-finding",
      "source": "review-2026-07-31 (reality-server segment, pm-backend expert)",
      "score_delta": 2,
      "confidence": "high",
      "candidate_vector": "bug",
      "evidence": "backend/servers/reality-server/src/routes/reports.rs:342 `let total = reports.len()` returns MyReportsResponse.total set to CURRENT-PAGE length after LIMIT/OFFSET applied (line 307). Default limit=20 (line 290), so a user with 100 reports always sees total: 20 on page 1; clients paginating by `total` stop early. Sibling endpoints do this correctly: articles.rs:196-208 (SELECT COUNT(*) with same filter) and saved_searches.rs:323-331 (`tokio::try_join!` page + count). Fix: run `SELECT COUNT(*)` alongside the page or use `COUNT(*) OVER ()` (see articles.rs:391)."
